\pard\ul\b 6\ulnone . Security Considetations\b0\par

\pard\li284 Any data compressing method involves the reduction of redudancy in the data. Consequently, any corruption of the ddata is likely to have severe effects and be difficult to correct. Uncompressed text, on the other hand, will probably still be readable descpite the presence of some corrupted bytes.\par
It is recommended that systems using this data format provide some means of validating the intefrity of the compressed data. See reference [\ul 3\ulnone ], for example.\f4\lang1049\par

